---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/national-investment.css';
---
<Base title="National Investment Atlas" description="An interactive 3D atlas of $71.019 billion in reported New Markets Tax Credit financing: geographic concentration, annual flows and metro/non-metro comparisons." wide={true}>
<div class="ni" id="national-investment">
  <nav class="ni-path" aria-label="Spatial work"><a href="/spatial/">Spatial &amp; 3D GIS</a><span>/</span><a href="/spatial-economics/">Asheville scenario</a><span>/</span><a href="/gis-portfolio/">Terrain &amp; reconstruction</a></nav>
  <header class="ni-heading"><div><p class="ni-kicker">SPATIAL INVESTMENT / UNITED STATES</p><h1>Where investment<br />takes place.</h1></div><p>New Markets Tax Credit financing across the United States and its territories. Compare regional concentration, inspect tract-level investment and trace each total to the public source.</p></header>
  <div class="ni-vintage"><span>OBSERVED FINANCING</span><span>2001–2023 origination years</span><span>CDFI release · August 2026</span><a href="#national-methods">Method &amp; coverage ↓</a></div>
  <section class="ni-controls" aria-label="Investment filters">
    <label>State or territory<select id="ni-state" disabled><option value="">United States &amp; territories</option></select></label>
    <fieldset><legend>Transaction origination</legend><label class="ni-sr" for="ni-from">First year</label><select id="ni-from" disabled>{Array.from({length:23},(_,i)=><option value={2001+i} selected={i===0}>{2001+i}</option>)}</select><span>to</span><label class="ni-sr" for="ni-to">Last year</label><select id="ni-to" disabled>{Array.from({length:23},(_,i)=><option value={2001+i} selected={i===22}>{2001+i}</option>)}</select></fieldset>
    <label>Project geography<select id="ni-metro" disabled><option value="">Metro &amp; non-metro</option><option>Metro</option><option>Non-Metro</option></select></label>
    <label>Reported QALICB type<select id="ni-type" disabled><option value="">All types</option><option value="NRE">Non-real estate (NRE)</option><option value="RE">Real estate (RE)</option><option value="SPE">SPE, as reported</option><option value="CDE">Other CDE</option></select></label>
    <button id="ni-reset" disabled>Reset filters</button>
  </section>
  <p id="ni-error" class="ni-notice" role="status">Loading the reconciled public data…</p>
  <section class="ni-metrics" aria-label="Selected investment" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
    <div><span>Reported QLICI financing</span><strong id="ni-total">$71.019B</strong><small>Nominal dollars · selected years</small></div>
    <div><span>Distinct projects financed</span><strong id="ni-count">8,439</strong><small>Counted once within the interval</small></div>
    <div><span>Non-metro financing share</span><strong id="ni-share">…</strong><small>Project-sheet classification</small></div>
    <div><span>Mean financing / project</span><strong id="ni-mean">…</strong><small>Selected financing / distinct projects</small></div>
  </section>
  <section class="ni-map-layout" aria-label="3D investment geography">
    <div class="ni-map-shell"><div id="ni-map" aria-label="3D map of reported investment"></div>
      <div class="ni-map-heading"><span id="ni-map-region">UNITED STATES</span><button id="ni-view" type="button">Reset view</button></div>
      <div class="ni-legend"><strong id="ni-map-unit">State &amp; territory totals</strong><span id="ni-height">Height: 100 km per $1 billion</span><span><i class="ni-metro-dot"></i> Metro majority <i class="ni-rural-dot"></i> Non-metro majority</span><span id="ni-point-note">Summary positions derived from financed tracts</span></div>
      <p id="ni-map-status" class="ni-map-status" role="status">Preparing 3D view. Tables remain available without WebGL.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="ni-inspector"><p class="ni-kicker">REGIONAL COMPARISON</p><h2 id="ni-selection-title">National distribution</h2><p id="ni-selection-description">Select a region in the table or on the globe to inspect its financed tracts.</p><div id="ni-selection-detail"></div>
      <p id="ni-coverage" class="ni-coverage"></p>
      <div class="ni-scale-note">Column heights encode financing. They do not represent buildings, estimated growth or the value of tax credits.</div>
      <a class="ni-scenario-link" href="/spatial-economics/">Model additionality &amp; access in Asheville ↗</a>
    </aside>
  </section>
  <section class="ni-history" aria-labelledby="ni-history-title"><div><p class="ni-kicker">TRANSACTION ORIGINATION</p><h2 id="ni-history-title">Financing over time</h2><p>Nominal annual financing within the selected geography and project types. Select a bar for that year; reset filters for the full period.</p></div><div id="ni-timeline" aria-label="Annual reported financing"></div></section>
  <div class="ni-tables">
    <section aria-labelledby="ni-regions-title"><div class="ni-section-head"><div><p class="ni-kicker">COMPARABLE TOTALS</p><h2 id="ni-regions-title">States &amp; territories</h2></div><span>Same years, geography class &amp; project types</span></div><p class="ni-table-note">Ranked by financing; totals are not normalized for population, economic size or eligible communities.</p><div class="ni-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Region</th><th scope="col">Financing</th><th scope="col">Projects</th><th scope="col">Non-metro</th></tr></thead><tbody id="ni-regions"></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="ni-projects-title"><div class="ni-section-head"><div><p class="ni-kicker">SOURCE RECORDS</p><h2 id="ni-projects-title">Projects in selection</h2></div><button id="ni-export" disabled>Export selection ↓</button></div><p class="ni-table-note" id="ni-record-count">Project identifiers from CDFI; geography is representative, not a site address.</p><div class="ni-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Project / city</th><th scope="col">2020 tract</th><th scope="col">Financing</th></tr></thead><tbody id="ni-projects"></tbody></table></div><div class="ni-pagination"><button id="ni-prev" disabled>Previous</button><span id="ni-page">…</span><button id="ni-next" disabled>Next</button></div></section>
  </div>
  <section class="ni-methods" id="national-methods"><div><p class="ni-kicker">METHOD / SOURCE AUDIT</p><h2>Observed financing and<br />the additionality question.</h2><p>The New Markets Tax Credit program channels financing through Community Development Entities. This atlas shows reported Qualified Low-Income Community Investments (QLICIs). Those amounts are neither federal tax expenditure nor a causal estimate of investment, employment or regional growth.</p><p>My <a href="/research/helfrich-2026-nmtc-rural-gap/">NMTC financing research</a> examines the rural financing gap using an earlier release through 2022. Its estimates and sample remain distinct from this updated descriptive atlas. The <a href="/spatial-economics/">Asheville model</a> explores additionality and spatial access under explicit assumptions.</p><div class="ni-source-links"><a href="/spatial-economics/national/sources.json">Source manifest ↗</a><a href="/spatial-economics/national/projects.json" download>Public analytical data ↓</a><a href="https://www.cdfifund.gov/documents/data-releases">CDFI release ↗</a></div></div>
    <div>
      <details open><summary>Reconciliation and time</summary><p>All 8,439 project totals reconcile exactly, to the cent, to 21,202 underlying transactions: $71,018,792,858.55. Financing is aggregated by transaction origination year. A project with transactions in several selected years is counted once. The annual chart counts its financing in each relevant year; summing annual project counts would double-count repeat projects.</p><p>The workbook contains origination years 2001–2023, including 2001 and 2002 despite “FY 2003–2023” in its title. Amounts are nominal reported dollars, not inflation-adjusted. This is a fixed August 2026 release, not a live program feed.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Representative tracts and missing locations</summary><p>Project-sheet 2020 tract identifiers join the Census Gazetteer’s internal points. These are locations within tracts, not building addresses or exact project coordinates. For multi-tract projects, the source selects a representative tract; this atlas assigns all project financing to that tract. It does not recover the entire investment footprint.</p><p>8,434 of 8,439 projects map successfully. Two American Samoa, two Guam and one U.S. Virgin Islands project lack a Gazetteer match. Their $45.2 million remains in totals, regional comparisons and exports. No substitute point is invented. National columns use fixed financing-weighted summary positions derived from matched tracts; select a state for tract detail. Alaska, Hawaii and Puerto Rico are available through the region selector.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Metro classification and borrower types</summary><p>Metro/non-metro follows the source’s project-sheet classification using 2020 tracts and March 2020 OMB definitions. It is held fixed for all transaction years; it is not a reconstruction of historical rural status or present eligibility. Reported type codes distinguish real estate (RE), non-real estate (NRE) and investments in another CDE. SPE is retained as reported; the release dictionary does not expand that code. Multi-CDE and multi-tract flags remain in exports.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Visual encodings and reproducibility</summary><p>National column height is 100 display kilometres per $1 billion; tract column height is 10 display kilometres per $10 million. Scales stay fixed when the year interval or project type changes. Teal indicates a majority of selected financing classified metro, gold a majority classified non-metro. Summary points with equal shares use teal. Columns encode nominal totals, not local economic impact, building heights or a surface estimate.</p><p>Each export contains the selected flows, project identities, representative geography, missing-location status, filter settings, source URLs and SHA-256 hashes. Exact cents drive aggregation; screen values are rounded. State outlines are cartographic context dissolved from the American Policy Atlas’s TIGER 2023 county geometry; they are not used for geographic assignment. <a href="/spatial-economics/national/context-sources.json">Outline provenance</a>. <a href="https://github.com/ihelfrich/ihelfrich.github.io/blob/main/scripts/spatial-economics/build_national.py">Reproducible source builder</a> and numerical tests are included in the website repository.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>
  <noscript><p>The interactive atlas requires JavaScript. The complete <a href="/spatial-economics/national/projects.json">project data</a> and <a href="/spatial-economics/national/sources.json">source audit</a> are available directly.</p></noscript>
</div>
<script>import '../../scripts/national-investment.mjs';</script>
</Base>
